1
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:41,560
Qian Yichuan.

2
00:00:42,159 --> 00:00:43,240
What happened to you?

3
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:44,600
Ma Guowen sent some thugs

4
00:00:45,359 --> 00:00:46,280
to beat him up.

5
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,960
While we were in the hospital,

6
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:50,640
they pried his dorm door open

7
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:52,359
and took the account books

8
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,560
along with all the evidence.

9
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:58,359
We came to see you today

10
00:00:59,039 --> 00:01:00,159
just to let you know,

11
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,320
about that documentary,

12
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:06,079
you must be under immense pressure.

13
00:01:08,319 --> 00:01:09,120
Still, we hope

14
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:11,120
you'll keep the record of our struggle

15
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:13,879
preserved for now.

16
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:15,519
The way things look now,

17
00:01:15,519 --> 00:01:17,200
it probably won't make it into a museum.

18
00:01:18,519 --> 00:01:19,079
Either way,

19
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:20,840
just keep it safe.

20
00:01:21,519 --> 00:01:22,840
Our kids can watch it someday,

21
00:01:23,719 --> 00:01:24,719
so they know when facing this,

22
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:27,200
we put up a fight.

23
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:29,680
We didn't just take it lying down.

24
00:01:34,359 --> 00:01:34,799
That's right.

25
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:39,680
We're all behind you.

26
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:40,519
Right.

27
00:01:40,519 --> 00:01:42,519
We all support you.

28
00:01:45,239 --> 00:01:46,799
We've all left the brewery now.

29
00:01:47,799 --> 00:01:48,719
We've got nothing left.

30
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:50,959
We're just counting on you

31
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,879
to edit the film,

32
00:01:54,439 --> 00:01:55,079
get it broadcast,

33
00:01:56,159 --> 00:01:57,280
and bring us some justice.

34
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,560
Justice will always prevail.

35
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,120
I won't give up.

36
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,319
Thank you, Reporter Shen.

37
00:02:15,199 --> 00:02:16,240
Sorry for putting you through this.

38
00:02:18,599 --> 00:02:19,120
Thank you.

39
00:02:19,199 --> 00:02:20,800
Thank you, Reporter Shen.

40
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:21,759
We all believe in you.

41
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:22,439
We all trust you.

42
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,000
We believe in you.

43
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:23,439
We're so grateful to you.

44
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:24,319
Please.

45
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:25,599
We're counting on you, Reporter Shen.

46
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:26,759
We believe in you.

47
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,879
Stop running off.

48
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:06,120
It'll get me in trouble.

49
00:04:12,759 --> 00:04:14,000
You never rest for a second, do you?

50
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:17,680
I'm pretty much fully recovered.

51
00:04:18,199 --> 00:04:19,439
Just getting ready to be discharged.

52
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,240
What about Li Mingyang,

53
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:22,600
and Sister Miao's situation?

54
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:23,720
Thanks.

55
00:04:24,519 --> 00:04:25,079
You're reinstated?

56
00:04:26,439 --> 00:04:27,800
If you're back on duty, go solve cases!

57
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:28,600
What are you doing here?

58
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:29,879
I am working a case.

59
00:04:29,879 --> 00:04:31,399
Dropped by to check on you, then I'm gone.

60
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,720
Pretty clever, aren't you?

61
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:35,959
What I have here

62
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,600
is called a trick up my sleeve.

63
00:04:40,279 --> 00:04:40,920
Shen Leshui...

64
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:43,120
smashed Li Mingyang's car, right?

65
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:44,160
It worked out great,

66
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:45,639
delivering Li Mingyang right to us.

67
00:04:46,279 --> 00:04:47,800
Right now, I'm playing the time gap.

68
00:04:47,959 --> 00:04:48,879
Li Mingyang is inside,

69
00:04:49,319 --> 00:04:50,759
and Miao Yuzhu is outside.

70
00:04:50,959 --> 00:04:52,279
I went to see Miao Yuzhu,

71
00:04:53,079 --> 00:04:54,920
to take them down one by one.

72
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,160
Let me tell you,

73
00:04:57,519 --> 00:04:59,160
anyone with a guilty conscience

74
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:01,360
always expects the worst from others.

75
00:05:03,519 --> 00:05:04,519
Let me teach you a trick.

76
00:05:04,879 --> 00:05:05,439
You know what this is?

77
00:05:05,439 --> 00:05:06,800
It's called the Prisoner's Dilemma.

78
00:05:07,079 --> 00:05:08,959
You set the hook right now,

79
00:05:09,279 --> 00:05:10,079
and the whole thing is solved.

80
00:05:12,279 --> 00:05:14,920
Qiang never taught you this, did he?

81
00:05:17,959 --> 00:05:18,800
Isn't this for me?

82
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:28,040
You think this is Shen Leshui's move?

83
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,079
If we were at a restaurant,

84
00:05:58,319 --> 00:05:59,560
we could've had a drink together.

85
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,519
Our squad has rules.

86
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:04,040
No drinking.

87
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:06,680
Right, I forgot.

88
00:06:07,279 --> 00:06:09,160
You're a stickler for rules.

89
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:10,519
Coming to visit you this time,

90
00:06:10,519 --> 00:06:11,959
I had approval from the higher-ups, you know.

91
00:06:13,199 --> 00:06:13,879
I get it, I get it.

92
00:06:14,399 --> 00:06:16,439
Next time I'll try to find a comfier spot,

93
00:06:17,079 --> 00:06:20,000
so you needn't apply to watch me stand.

94
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,839
Sounds like you never had to stand.

95
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,519
Must've been a model student growing up.

96
00:06:24,959 --> 00:06:25,519
Have a seat.

97
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,160
I forgive you.

98
00:06:55,199 --> 00:06:56,600
I haven't even apologized.

99
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:06,199
The reason I couldn't

100
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:08,519
let Liu Xuemei's death go...

101
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,439
is because that day,

102
00:07:13,079 --> 00:07:14,680
she rode in my father's car

103
00:07:15,959 --> 00:07:17,879
from Qingzhou to Lacheng.

104
00:07:20,879 --> 00:07:22,079
I remember it so clearly.

105
00:07:22,439 --> 00:07:24,040
It was snowing heavily that morning.

106
00:07:25,879 --> 00:07:27,959
I watched his little red car

107
00:07:30,279 --> 00:07:31,319
get farther and farther away,

108
00:07:31,519 --> 00:07:32,319
farther and farther.

109
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,120
I was holding up a meat bun,

110
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,439
wanting him to eat it before leaving.

111
00:07:43,639 --> 00:07:44,959
I couldn't stop him.

112
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:57,519
That very night, he

113
00:07:59,399 --> 00:08:00,000
died.

114
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,319
Along with Liu Xuemei.

115
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,959
Both causes of death were tied to alcohol.

116
00:08:08,959 --> 00:08:10,279
Liu Xuemei

117
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:14,319
froze to death from drunken hypothermia.

118
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,240
My father was

119
00:08:17,759 --> 00:08:19,079
drunk driving.

120
00:08:19,519 --> 00:08:20,319
A car crash.

121
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,680
My dad drove a taxi.

122
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:32,840
To stay ready for work,

123
00:08:34,879 --> 00:08:36,039
he never touched a drop.

124
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:39,639
Not a single drop!

125
00:08:40,799 --> 00:08:42,759
Liu Xuemei was a Beer Taster.

126
00:08:42,759 --> 00:08:45,519
To keep her sense of taste sharp,

127
00:08:46,679 --> 00:08:47,600
she couldn't drink either.

128
00:08:51,759 --> 00:08:53,120
Two people who never drank

129
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:56,320
died drunk on the very same day.

130
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:57,519
Isn't that strange?

131
00:08:57,879 --> 00:08:59,039
Shouldn't it be investigated?

132
00:09:04,519 --> 00:09:05,240
I'm sorry.

133
00:09:18,519 --> 00:09:19,440
Just this one thing.

134
00:09:22,879 --> 00:09:23,919
Just this one thing.

135
00:09:25,879 --> 00:09:28,519
I've thought about it since I was eight.

136
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,960
It's been like a mountain,

137
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:37,320
weighing on my chest for over a decade.

138
00:09:51,159 --> 00:09:52,080
So you suspect me,

139
00:09:52,159 --> 00:09:53,159
you think I'm acting weird.

140
00:09:53,159 --> 00:09:53,879
I guess...

141
00:09:54,679 --> 00:09:55,360
that makes sense.

142
00:09:58,919 --> 00:09:59,559
You...

143
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:01,759
becoming a cop...

144
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:03,840
does it have to do with this, too—

145
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,039
Me becoming a cop,

146
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:07,519
from Qingzhou to Lacheng,

147
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:09,600
every single thing,

148
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,120
just... just...

149
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:10,799
all of this,

150
00:10:10,799 --> 00:10:12,000
it's all tied to this.

151
00:10:16,679 --> 00:10:18,159
I want to find the truth.

152
00:10:21,279 --> 00:10:22,639
Ever since Ma Guowen died,

153
00:10:22,639 --> 00:10:24,679
I feel I'm getting closer to the truth.

154
00:10:27,159 --> 00:10:28,320
I will definitely find it.

155
00:10:39,799 --> 00:10:40,360
By the way,

156
00:10:40,919 --> 00:10:42,720
I looked into that threat letter.

157
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:44,919
It wasn't Li Mingyang or Miao Yuzhu.

158
00:10:45,399 --> 00:10:46,360
No need to check.

159
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,919
It actually works in my favor.

160
00:10:50,159 --> 00:10:52,639
If I'm just the one who reported it,

161
00:10:53,679 --> 00:10:56,279
I won't get to touch the case again.

162
00:10:57,039 --> 00:10:59,200
But if another case involves me,

163
00:11:00,279 --> 00:11:02,039
I'll have a chance to stay close to you

164
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,720
and find out more.

165
00:11:09,799 --> 00:11:11,039
Why would you do that?

166
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:12,720
When people run into a homicide,

167
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:14,080
they can't get away fast enough.

168
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,759
Why do you keep throwing yourself into it?

169
00:11:21,759 --> 00:11:22,879
Is this your...

170
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:25,159
journalistic instinct,

171
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:27,360
or... or is it...

172
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:28,759
or did you...

173
00:11:28,759 --> 00:11:29,919
Did you smell money?

174
00:11:33,159 --> 00:11:34,799
I know you're selling your house.

175
00:11:34,799 --> 00:11:36,000
I know you're broke.

176
00:11:40,759 --> 00:11:41,200
I...

177
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,200
I admit it.

178
00:11:44,519 --> 00:11:45,320
Lately...

179
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,519
I've really been strapped for cash.

180
00:11:51,679 --> 00:11:53,080
Everyone goes through tough times.

181
00:11:57,879 --> 00:12:00,360
The day before I came back to Lacheng,

182
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,759
I spent my 40th birthday all alone.

183
00:12:09,799 --> 00:12:11,039
Drowning in debt,

184
00:12:11,039 --> 00:12:12,480
with no idea how to pay it off.

185
00:12:18,519 --> 00:12:19,399
For months,

186
00:12:20,559 --> 00:12:22,600
I haven't made a single dime.

187
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,000
Rent went up again,

188
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:28,919
and I couldn't afford it.

189
00:12:33,759 --> 00:12:35,000
Everyone has it rough.

190
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:39,240
Who'd help a worthless guy

191
00:12:39,519 --> 00:12:40,559
get through a crisis?

192
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,519
That night, I made up my mind

193
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:50,159
to give up those unrealistic dreams.

194
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:52,840
As long as I can pay off the debt, it's fine.

195
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,000
So I returned to Lacheng to sell my place.

196
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:00,320
Right after coming back, I ran into Ma Guowen.

197
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:04,320
I thought I hit the jackpot.

198
00:13:06,639 --> 00:13:07,720
I must've been out of my mind.

199
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,799
40 years old.

200
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,559
At 30, you stand on your own.

201
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:28,960
At 40, you have no doubts.

202
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:31,840
What about at 50?

203
00:13:35,279 --> 00:13:35,639
Come on,

204
00:13:35,639 --> 00:13:37,279
who came up with these numbers anyway?

205
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:40,759
If you ask me,

206
00:13:40,919 --> 00:13:42,039
as long as you're alive,

207
00:13:42,519 --> 00:13:43,840
and as long as you still have desires,

208
00:13:44,879 --> 00:13:46,519
you'll always be confused at any age.

209
00:13:48,639 --> 00:13:49,440
Or in trouble.

210
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,679
I mean the kind you bring on yourself.

211
00:13:53,639 --> 00:13:54,840
First, you're confused,

212
00:13:55,879 --> 00:13:56,840
and then...

213
00:13:57,519 --> 00:13:58,240
you run into deep trouble.

214
00:14:03,879 --> 00:14:05,519
Misfortune may be a blessing in disguise.

215
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:06,519
Look at it from another angle.

216
00:14:06,519 --> 00:14:07,519
Maybe it's a good thing.

217
00:14:07,759 --> 00:14:09,120
Don't bother comforting me.

218
00:14:10,879 --> 00:14:12,360
I've had so much bad luck,

219
00:14:12,639 --> 00:14:13,279
I'm used to it.

220
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,120
Shen Leshui.

221
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,240
I gave you this assignment in the first place

222
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,919
to give a young person like you a chance,

223
00:14:34,399 --> 00:14:35,519
and because you told me

224
00:14:35,559 --> 00:14:37,000
you'd capture the workers' smiling faces.

225
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:37,879
You duped me!

226
00:14:38,159 --> 00:14:39,159
Once this film airs,

227
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:40,639
our station's

228
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:43,559
our yearly ad revenue goes down the drain!

229
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:44,360
Director,

230
00:14:44,879 --> 00:14:45,879
when I said smiling faces,

231
00:14:45,879 --> 00:14:47,799
I meant the true face of the workers.

232
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,279
Don't give me that "truth" crap!

233
00:14:49,519 --> 00:14:50,360
What is "truth"?

234
00:14:50,919 --> 00:14:52,360
Ma Guowen is still

235
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:54,039
the head of Lapi Brewery.

236
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,320
That's the truth!

237
00:14:56,639 --> 00:14:57,080
Right now,

238
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:57,720
print media,

239
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:58,399
radio,

240
00:14:58,399 --> 00:15:00,679
and TV stations are in fierce competition!

241
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:03,080
It's a battlefield without smoke!

242
00:15:03,519 --> 00:15:04,320
Yet look at you!

243
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:06,399
A client we nurtured for so many years,

244
00:15:06,399 --> 00:15:07,559
such a valuable client,

245
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,720
and you just drove them away!

246
00:15:08,919 --> 00:15:09,519
Seriously,

247
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:11,080
who sent you?

248
00:15:11,519 --> 00:15:12,399
Are you an undercover mole?

249
00:15:13,639 --> 00:15:14,200
Director,

250
00:15:14,399 --> 00:15:16,159
you can't just care about commercial profits.

251
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:18,759
Let me tell you,

252
00:15:19,519 --> 00:15:20,200
Lapi Brewery

253
00:15:20,399 --> 00:15:21,720
is the pride of our entire city.

254
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,759
It's not something you can just smear!

255
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:24,879
Discordant voices

256
00:15:25,519 --> 00:15:26,679
cannot appear in this film!

257
00:15:28,679 --> 00:15:29,240
Come in!

258
00:15:31,399 --> 00:15:32,519
Miao Yuzhu, get over here!

259
00:15:33,639 --> 00:15:34,639
Have you lost your mind too?

260
00:15:35,399 --> 00:15:36,519
Giving her the tapes without permission!

261
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:38,120
I'm docking your bonus for the whole year!

262
00:15:38,639 --> 00:15:39,840
Director, don't blame Xiao Miao.

263
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,519
I asked her for them.

264
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:42,840
Dock my bonus instead!

265
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,120
Shen Leshui,

266
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,279
I'll give you one more chance.

267
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,120
Follow my script

268
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:50,879
and re-edit it.

269
00:15:51,759 --> 00:15:53,039
No sneaking in your personal agenda!

270
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:54,159
Also,

271
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:56,720
the thirty tapes approved by the station,

272
00:15:57,279 --> 00:15:58,039
plus the three

273
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,159
Xiao Miao gave you without permission...

274
00:15:59,399 --> 00:16:00,120
Once you're done editing,

275
00:16:00,279 --> 00:16:01,000
hand them all over!

276
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:02,759
And whatever you shot yourself,

277
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:04,080
turn that in as well.

278
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,279
Someone else paid for those.

279
00:16:07,799 --> 00:16:08,440
I don't have them.

280
00:16:08,879 --> 00:16:09,759
Can't hand them over.

281
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:10,519
You...!

282
00:16:15,159 --> 00:16:15,720
Fine.

283
00:16:16,279 --> 00:16:17,200
You must guarantee

284
00:16:17,519 --> 00:16:19,000
they never leak out.

285
00:16:19,519 --> 00:16:20,879
Go back and write a letter of commitment.

286
00:16:21,639 --> 00:16:22,360
Let me tell you,

287
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,279
if any tape leaks,

288
00:16:24,639 --> 00:16:25,639
you take full responsibility!

289
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:37,200
Watch from the back and learn.

290
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:40,279
Cut this whole section.

291
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:43,240
We can keep this.

292
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,360
Who asked you?

293
00:16:45,519 --> 00:16:46,519
Are you accountable to the station,

294
00:16:46,519 --> 00:16:47,679
or am I?

295
00:16:48,159 --> 00:16:48,799
Out, out, out.

296
00:16:49,159 --> 00:16:49,759
Director...

297
00:16:49,759 --> 00:16:50,279
We really can keep this.

298
00:16:50,279 --> 00:16:51,159
This is just great.

299
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:51,799
Get out.

300
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:24,839
Liu Tieping.

301
00:17:25,519 --> 00:17:26,400
What is it?

302
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:27,720
My master and the others are here.

303
00:17:29,359 --> 00:17:30,079
They're here, they're here.

304
00:17:30,119 --> 00:17:30,680
Come on.

305
00:17:30,839 --> 00:17:31,519
Listen to me, okay?

306
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:33,839
Master.

307
00:17:34,799 --> 00:17:35,440
Xiao Shen.

308
00:17:36,039 --> 00:17:36,839
Off work?

309
00:17:37,599 --> 00:17:38,279
Director Cheng.

310
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:40,759
Everyone's here.

311
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,599
All of us fellow workers...

312
00:17:42,759 --> 00:17:43,759
...have been worried about you.

313
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:45,559
Wanted to check in on you.

314
00:17:45,599 --> 00:17:46,240
Check in on you.

315
00:17:48,839 --> 00:17:49,680
What's wrong?

316
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:53,160
You seem a bit down.

317
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:54,359
It's nothing.

318
00:17:55,799 --> 00:17:56,519
It's just...

319
00:17:58,519 --> 00:18:01,160
They sent someone to edit *Malt Kingdom*.

320
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,039
After all...

321
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:04,839
it's my first time working solo.

322
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:08,240
I don't have the final cut.

323
00:18:09,119 --> 00:18:10,319
What does that mean?

324
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:11,599
Yeah, what does that mean?

325
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,799
I get it, I get it.

326
00:18:15,319 --> 00:18:16,440
We all understand.

327
00:18:17,799 --> 00:18:18,880
The station bosses...

328
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:20,039
...want this film...

329
00:18:20,119 --> 00:18:20,720
...to turn out well.

330
00:18:21,039 --> 00:18:21,440
Right?

331
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:22,119
Turn out well.

332
00:18:22,319 --> 00:18:22,720
Right.

333
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:23,559
Got it.

334
00:18:23,559 --> 00:18:24,319
Understood, understood.

335
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,519
The reason we all came today...

336
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,039
...is to ask you...

337
00:18:30,039 --> 00:18:31,200
...about buying the factory...

338
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:33,160
...well...

339
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,519
...don't put it in the film.

340
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:35,519
Can you do that?

341
00:18:35,839 --> 00:18:36,400
Leave it out.

342
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:37,039
Right, right, right.

343
00:18:37,039 --> 00:18:37,519
Leave it out.

344
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:38,640
Qian Yichuan...

345
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:39,880
...and Tu Chunyan are different.

346
00:18:40,359 --> 00:18:41,359
They've got nothing to lose.

347
00:18:42,039 --> 00:18:42,519
But us...

348
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:44,519
...us frontline workers...

349
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:45,519
...we can't take that hit.

350
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:46,880
If...

351
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:49,400
...once your piece airs...

352
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:51,200
...even active workers will be laid off.

353
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:52,599
And those already laid off...

354
00:18:52,839 --> 00:18:54,279
...who would dare hire them?

355
00:18:54,559 --> 00:18:55,559
"Just a bunch of troublemakers."

356
00:18:55,559 --> 00:18:56,119
Right?

357
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:58,519
Look...

358
00:18:58,640 --> 00:18:59,880
I can't lose my job.

359
00:19:00,279 --> 00:19:01,599
I rely on this paycheck.

360
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:03,400
If I get laid off...

361
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,119
...how am I supposed to survive?

362
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:05,599
Exactly.

363
00:19:05,599 --> 00:19:06,640
I can't be laid off either.

364
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:08,440
Reporter Shen, my family relies on me!

365
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:09,000
Quiet down!

366
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:09,799
That factory buyout...

367
00:19:09,839 --> 00:19:10,799
...please don't put it in the film.

368
00:19:10,799 --> 00:19:11,519
Please leave it out.

369
00:19:11,519 --> 00:19:12,839
Reporter Shen, please help us out.

370
00:19:14,079 --> 00:19:14,519
Thank you so much.

371
00:19:14,519 --> 00:19:15,119
Take these eggs.

372
00:19:15,519 --> 00:19:16,279
Please take them, take them.

373
00:19:16,279 --> 00:19:17,240
We're counting on you.

374
00:19:17,279 --> 00:19:18,160
Please, we're begging you.

375
00:19:18,279 --> 00:19:19,079
Just let it slide.

376
00:19:19,079 --> 00:19:20,319
We can't lose this job.

377
00:19:20,319 --> 00:19:20,799
Understood.

378
00:19:20,799 --> 00:19:21,279
Yes.

379
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:22,400
Quiet down, quiet down.

380
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,240
Reporter Shen surely understands.

381
00:19:25,519 --> 00:19:26,240
He knows what to do.

382
00:19:26,599 --> 00:19:27,920
We know you're a good person.

383
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:28,839
Thanks for your hard work, Reporter Shen.

384
00:19:28,839 --> 00:19:29,440
Get some rest.

385
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:31,000
Thank you, thank you.

386
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,839
When *Malt Kingdom* won that award,

387
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,359
I cried my eyes out.

388
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:43,960
People thought it was from excitement,

389
00:19:45,319 --> 00:19:46,680
but I was truly heartbroken.

390
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:50,680
Heartbroken for those

391
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:53,039
who had placed their hopes in me,

392
00:19:54,319 --> 00:19:55,559
and for myself.

393
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:01,839
So at that moment, I swore

394
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:04,160
I'd definitely become a director

395
00:20:04,559 --> 00:20:06,160
who had final cut.

396
00:20:07,359 --> 00:20:09,680
I've worked toward that all these years.

397
00:20:10,640 --> 00:20:12,559
Never thought I'd get burned so badly.

398
00:20:12,559 --> 00:20:13,319
At my age,

399
00:20:13,319 --> 00:20:14,880
getting fooled by some petty thief.

400
00:20:20,759 --> 00:20:21,880
Easy, easy, don't get worked up.

401
00:20:24,319 --> 00:20:25,599
Petty thieves these days,

402
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:26,440
these young punks,

403
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:29,359
their minds really do move fast.

404
00:20:30,039 --> 00:20:31,119
When we get older,

405
00:20:31,119 --> 00:20:33,119
we just can't keep up with them.

406
00:20:42,359 --> 00:20:43,599
What am I even saying?

407
00:20:46,799 --> 00:20:47,599
I'm sorry.

408
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:52,079
It's in the past.

409
00:20:53,319 --> 00:20:54,359
What's done is done.

410
00:20:54,759 --> 00:20:55,279
Alright?

411
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:58,400
My grandma always had a saying:

412
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:00,400
always remember people's kindness,

413
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,160
and don't hold grudges.

414
00:21:05,039 --> 00:21:05,880
Grandma Gao...

415
00:21:08,039 --> 00:21:10,519
I lied to her that day, too.

416
00:21:16,039 --> 00:21:18,000
You? Your mental age

417
00:21:18,279 --> 00:21:19,400
is seventeen or eighteen at best.

418
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:22,680
You think you could fool her?

419
00:21:23,279 --> 00:21:24,599
The minute you walked out that day,

420
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:26,400
she called me right up.

421
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:28,240
She told me to watch out for you,

422
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:30,119
said you didn't look like a good guy.

423
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,039
Let me tell you,

424
00:21:36,519 --> 00:21:39,079
the people's eyes are sharp.

425
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:41,440
My grandma might be old,

426
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,279
can barely read the words,

427
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,720
but she's never wrong about people.

428
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:54,640
All right.

429
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:57,240
Feel better getting that off your chest?

430
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,680
Done venting?

431
00:22:04,839 --> 00:22:06,119
I'll take off then.

432
00:22:06,359 --> 00:22:08,039
I've got a million other things to check.

433
00:22:08,799 --> 00:22:10,799
I'll keep looking into that threat letter.

434
00:22:11,279 --> 00:22:12,200
After all, you did report it.

435
00:22:13,519 --> 00:22:14,359
Gao.

436
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:16,839
Over a decade ago...

437
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:19,519
I got a threatening letter, too.

438
00:22:21,279 --> 00:22:21,880
Shen.

439
00:22:22,119 --> 00:22:22,920
There's a letter here for you.

440
00:22:23,599 --> 00:22:24,440
Thanks, sir.

441
00:22:36,039 --> 00:22:36,880
Who threatened you?

442
00:23:21,519 --> 00:23:22,559
You're unbelievable.

443
00:23:23,359 --> 00:23:24,359
You took what happened back then

444
00:23:24,359 --> 00:23:25,440
and sold it out for cash, didn't you?

445
00:23:34,119 --> 00:23:35,400
Over ten years ago,

446
00:23:36,119 --> 00:23:37,000
right in front of this door,

447
00:23:37,599 --> 00:23:38,759
we trusted you once.

448
00:23:40,559 --> 00:23:41,559
And now,

449
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,559
I trusted you again.

450
00:23:44,599 --> 00:23:46,519
Do you think we're just a bunch of suckers

451
00:23:46,519 --> 00:23:47,440
you can fool whenever you want?

452
00:23:47,559 --> 00:23:48,759
Think we're easy targets?

453
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:50,759
Sell your house and get the hell out.

454
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:52,559
I never want to see you again.

455
00:23:54,359 --> 00:23:55,279
I'm sorry.

456
00:23:56,279 --> 00:23:57,119
Hypocrite.

457
00:23:57,680 --> 00:23:59,160
Do you have any shame at all?

458
00:23:59,400 --> 00:23:59,839
Get out!

459
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:01,720
Are you even human?

460
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:32,680
Cheng.

461
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:34,200
Introduce yourself.

462
00:24:34,319 --> 00:24:34,759
Okay.

463
00:24:36,519 --> 00:24:37,759
I'm Cheng Youtian,

464
00:24:38,519 --> 00:24:40,079
head of the bottling workshop.

465
00:24:43,319 --> 00:24:44,759
I'm Liu Xuemei.

466
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:46,680
I'm 32 years old,

467
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:50,160
a Beer Taster at state-owned Lapi Brewery.

468
00:24:50,599 --> 00:24:52,119
As a Beer Taster,

469
00:24:52,519 --> 00:24:54,319
our job is very important.

470
00:24:54,519 --> 00:24:55,920
Normally, I can't drink alcohol,

471
00:24:56,519 --> 00:24:57,720
or eat heavily seasoned

472
00:24:57,799 --> 00:24:59,039
or spicy food.

473
00:25:00,039 --> 00:25:01,599
Not that I like that stuff anyway.

474
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:06,559
I really care about my coworkers.

475
00:25:07,279 --> 00:25:09,240
They're like family to me.

476
00:25:09,359 --> 00:25:11,359
And I really love our brewery.

477
00:25:13,759 --> 00:25:14,680
What else should I say?

478
00:25:15,359 --> 00:25:15,920
Whatever you like.

479
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:17,039
What else is there?

480
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:20,279
Talk about your dreams, your hobbies...

481
00:25:20,279 --> 00:25:21,519
your hopes for the factory.

482
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:22,519
Anything at all.

483
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:24,440
Go on.

484
00:25:24,559 --> 00:25:25,640
What kind of dreams could I have?

485
00:25:27,279 --> 00:25:29,319
I just hope my son

486
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:30,519
gets good grades on his finals.

487
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:33,039
He... He's eight this year.

488
00:25:33,119 --> 00:25:35,240
I hope he gets into college someday.

489
00:25:38,720 --> 00:25:39,640
That's wonderful.

490
00:25:40,119 --> 00:25:41,160
Leave this to Xuemei.

491
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:42,000
Consider it done.

492
00:25:42,039 --> 00:25:42,720
Right, right.

493
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:43,759
All right, then.

494
00:25:43,759 --> 00:25:44,920
Stop arguing with them.

495
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:45,519
Let's pack it up.

496
00:25:45,519 --> 00:25:46,000
Okay.

497
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:46,839
Tell everyone to head back.

498
00:25:47,559 --> 00:25:48,039
Got it.

499
00:26:15,599 --> 00:26:16,599
Let go of me. I get it.

500
00:26:16,599 --> 00:26:17,160
Okay.

501
00:26:17,160 --> 00:26:17,720
Let's go.

502
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:33,319
Chen Yuan.

503
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:35,559
What are you doing?

504
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:37,119
You're back.

505
00:26:37,839 --> 00:26:38,319
I'm

506
00:26:38,839 --> 00:26:39,680
looking for a book.

507
00:26:40,119 --> 00:26:41,039
A book?

508
00:26:43,359 --> 00:26:44,440
I bought beef pies.

509
00:26:44,680 --> 00:26:45,519
Eat them while they're hot.

510
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:47,160
Okay, I'll be right there.

511
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:49,200
Come on, Xiaohu.

512
00:26:49,200 --> 00:26:50,319
Go wash your hands first.

513
00:26:50,359 --> 00:26:51,519
I'll find your toy train in a bit.

514
00:27:33,559 --> 00:27:34,279
Who is it?

515
00:27:34,359 --> 00:27:34,880
It's me.

516
00:28:06,119 --> 00:28:07,400
I never would've thought

517
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:11,559
a big reporter like you could get conned.

518
00:28:12,559 --> 00:28:13,319
Let me tell you,

519
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:14,759
that little bastard better not show his face.

520
00:28:15,519 --> 00:28:16,759
I'll smack him every time I see him.

521
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:19,519
That woman across the hall, too.

522
00:28:21,079 --> 00:28:21,880
She better stay out of my sight.

523
00:28:35,519 --> 00:28:36,440
I kept telling you to leave,

524
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:38,240
but you just refused.

525
00:28:40,240 --> 00:28:41,079
Let me tell you,

526
00:28:41,880 --> 00:28:42,880
in this world,

527
00:28:43,039 --> 00:28:44,759
if anyone truly cares about you,

528
00:28:45,839 --> 00:28:46,519
it's your mom.

529
00:28:47,319 --> 00:28:48,160
And after her, it's me.

530
00:28:55,599 --> 00:28:56,559
So you won't leave, huh?

531
00:28:58,039 --> 00:28:58,599
Right.

532
00:29:03,519 --> 00:29:04,200
Fine, then.

533
00:29:06,279 --> 00:29:08,559
We may not be family on paper,

534
00:29:09,720 --> 00:29:11,920
but I'll always look out for you.

535
00:29:13,680 --> 00:29:14,240
I've made up my mind.

536
00:29:15,759 --> 00:29:17,000
Starting today,

537
00:29:18,160 --> 00:29:19,000
wherever you go,

538
00:29:19,359 --> 00:29:20,119
I go.

539
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:21,319
I'm staying right here.

540
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:23,839
Don't "what" me!

541
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:26,000
If bad guys show up, I'll take them on.

542
00:29:26,319 --> 00:29:27,839
Worst case, we fight to the death.

543
00:29:28,119 --> 00:29:28,680
What's the big deal?

544
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,519
I... I'm fine now.

545
00:29:31,559 --> 00:29:32,200
I'm fine.

546
00:29:32,519 --> 00:29:33,599
Just... just hurry home.

547
00:29:33,599 --> 00:29:34,640
Just stay by Lili's side.

548
00:29:35,200 --> 00:29:36,000
Don't worry about Lili.

549
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:37,799
I took her to her parents' place.

550
00:29:39,799 --> 00:29:41,640
Then you definitely can't stay here.

551
00:29:41,920 --> 00:29:43,079
Just go. Get out of here.

552
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,519
Don't make things harder for me.

553
00:29:45,240 --> 00:29:46,720
How am I making things harder?

554
00:29:47,079 --> 00:29:48,240
I'll take the couch,

555
00:29:48,839 --> 00:29:49,799
and you take the bed.

556
00:29:50,680 --> 00:29:51,240
It's fine.

557
00:29:56,680 --> 00:29:57,440
Haipeng,

558
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:00,240
thank you.

559
00:30:02,079 --> 00:30:02,720
I know that

560
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:05,240
besides my mom,

561
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:07,720
you're the last person who'd ever hurt me.

562
00:30:09,799 --> 00:30:11,799
That's why I hope you understand:

563
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:14,640
I have to see this case through.

564
00:30:17,200 --> 00:30:19,039
Because over a decade ago, I backed down

565
00:30:20,079 --> 00:30:21,359
and let so many people down.

566
00:30:22,599 --> 00:30:23,599
Falling for this deception

567
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,319
let you all down again.

568
00:30:27,440 --> 00:30:28,920
That slap from Tu Chunyan...

569
00:30:29,400 --> 00:30:30,519
I had it coming.

570
00:30:33,160 --> 00:30:34,920
So much I still haven't figured out.

571
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:37,440
Like Liu Xuemei.

572
00:30:38,640 --> 00:30:40,720
I really don't know if she was wronged.

573
00:30:41,559 --> 00:30:43,519
So no matter what, I have to stay here.

574
00:30:43,839 --> 00:30:45,000
Even if the killer comes after me,

575
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:46,359
I'll demand to know why.

576
00:30:56,799 --> 00:30:58,839
If only we could turn back time.

577
00:31:01,559 --> 00:31:03,200
None of this would've happened.

578
00:31:10,839 --> 00:31:12,759
Too bad you can't turn back time.

579
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:17,359
Right now,

580
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:19,720
that you trust me

581
00:31:20,720 --> 00:31:21,640
and I trust you...

582
00:31:23,319 --> 00:31:24,519
that's already rare enough.

583
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:29,799
Go on home.

584
00:31:31,599 --> 00:31:32,759
I'll lock the door.

585
00:31:35,319 --> 00:31:35,960
Don't worry.

586
00:31:39,079 --> 00:31:39,680
Head back inside.

587
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:49,200
Call me if anything comes up.

588
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:52,640
Go on.

589
00:31:54,759 --> 00:31:55,799
Don't go out unless you have to.

590
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:00,519
I'm heading out.

591
00:32:11,359 --> 00:32:12,559
Make sure to lock the door.

592
00:32:13,720 --> 00:32:14,519
You be careful too.

593
00:32:55,200 --> 00:32:56,039
What did they steal?

594
00:32:56,440 --> 00:32:57,920
Discarded footage from Lapi Brewery.

595
00:33:46,079 --> 00:33:46,799
Chen Yuan.

596
00:33:48,039 --> 00:33:48,720
What are you doing?

597
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:50,559
You're back.

598
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:51,720
I'm...

599
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:53,079
looking for a book.

600
00:34:06,079 --> 00:34:08,400
Who actually killed Cao Jun?

601
00:34:09,719 --> 00:34:10,719
Cheng Youtian.

602
00:34:12,079 --> 00:34:13,320
When Cao Jun was killed,

603
00:34:13,320 --> 00:34:15,639
he chatted with a pal at the gas station.

604
00:34:17,119 --> 00:34:19,519
When Liu Tieping was killed,

605
00:34:19,519 --> 00:34:21,800
he was drinking with Li San and the rest.

606
00:34:23,239 --> 00:34:24,519
Chen Qingchun.

607
00:34:25,119 --> 00:34:26,679
He crashed into the big sculpture back then.

608
00:34:27,639 --> 00:34:28,679
Zhao Haipeng.

609
00:34:30,119 --> 00:34:31,760
When the crime happened, Zhao Haipeng

610
00:34:31,760 --> 00:34:34,320
playing mahjong with wife and neighbors.

611
00:34:35,679 --> 00:34:37,440
They all have alibis.

612
00:34:38,360 --> 00:34:42,639
Could the killer be someone off our radar?

613
00:34:47,280 --> 00:34:47,920
Xiaoqin.

614
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:49,039
What brings you here?

615
00:34:55,119 --> 00:34:55,880
What's wrong?

616
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:58,360
The stuff you left at my place,

617
00:34:59,280 --> 00:35:00,440
and the discarded footage you threw away,

618
00:35:02,199 --> 00:35:02,960
are all here.

619
00:35:16,840 --> 00:35:17,679
None missing, right?

620
00:35:18,119 --> 00:35:19,280
Give the tapes back to me.

621
00:35:19,840 --> 00:35:20,880
Does Chen Yuan know?

622
00:35:24,679 --> 00:35:25,360
These tapes of yours,

623
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:26,320
stored for so many years,

624
00:35:27,199 --> 00:35:28,159
could they be damaged?

625
00:35:28,400 --> 00:35:28,920
No.

626
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,519
I've been watching them every day.

627
00:35:30,679 --> 00:35:31,719
These tapes here,

628
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:32,800
they're damaged.

629
00:35:33,039 --> 00:35:34,159
I marked them for you.

630
00:35:34,199 --> 00:35:34,960
Damaged?

631
00:36:03,599 --> 00:36:05,199
Why erase my tapes?

632
00:36:09,559 --> 00:36:10,800
When did you find out?

633
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:12,920
Does it matter when I found out?

634
00:36:16,519 --> 00:36:17,079
Leshui,

635
00:36:18,599 --> 00:36:19,519
tell me.

636
00:36:20,519 --> 00:36:22,519
Why did Chen Yuan steal your tapes?

637
00:36:23,079 --> 00:36:25,559
Why did he have to delete things from them?

638
00:36:26,719 --> 00:36:27,920
Why?

639
00:36:33,679 --> 00:36:35,679
He's the man who lies beside me every day.

640
00:36:36,559 --> 00:36:38,199
He's Xiaohu's father,

641
00:36:41,280 --> 00:36:42,800
the father of my child.

642
00:36:46,199 --> 00:36:48,000
I've known him for so many years,

643
00:36:50,199 --> 00:36:51,599
and I never imagined

644
00:36:52,320 --> 00:36:54,119
he could be such a terrifying person.

645
00:36:56,360 --> 00:36:56,960
Leshui,

646
00:36:57,639 --> 00:36:58,280
tell me,

647
00:36:58,280 --> 00:36:59,559
what am I supposed to do?

648
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:03,639
What should I do, Leshui?

649
00:37:18,800 --> 00:37:19,559
Slow down.

650
00:37:21,719 --> 00:37:22,159
Did you eat?

651
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:26,599
Chen Yuan.

652
00:37:39,079 --> 00:37:39,760
Shen Leshui.

653
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:40,880
What are you doing here?

654
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:43,400
I came to see you.

655
00:37:44,119 --> 00:37:44,719
Me?

656
00:37:46,880 --> 00:37:47,920
To talk about the tape.

657
00:37:52,159 --> 00:37:52,960
Get in the car.

658
00:38:13,400 --> 00:38:15,840
You took advantage of me seeing Xiaoqin

659
00:38:15,840 --> 00:38:16,760
to break into my place,

660
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:19,079
steal the tapes,

661
00:38:19,440 --> 00:38:20,440
and delete the surveillance footage.

662
00:38:21,679 --> 00:38:22,719
Several tapes of raw footage...

663
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:24,039
you even erased them.

664
00:38:26,039 --> 00:38:27,760
The police are on their way right now.

665
00:38:31,119 --> 00:38:32,239
I asked to meet you here

666
00:38:32,639 --> 00:38:34,800
because I didn't want the kid and Xiaoqin

667
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:35,920
to see you get taken away by the cops.

668
00:38:38,599 --> 00:38:40,159
Let's save each other some face

669
00:38:40,760 --> 00:38:42,280
and lay everything out in the open.

670
00:38:42,920 --> 00:38:43,559
All right?

671
00:38:56,440 --> 00:38:58,519
The 1999 Lapi Brewery beer label.

672
00:38:59,000 --> 00:38:59,679
An angel.

673
00:39:02,920 --> 00:39:03,800
Looks familiar, doesn't it?

674
00:39:05,719 --> 00:39:07,119
This beautiful side profile...

675
00:39:07,199 --> 00:39:08,519
reminds me of someone.

676
00:39:10,039 --> 00:39:11,039
Liu Xuemei.

677
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:16,880
To paint Liu Xuemei so beautifully,

678
00:39:18,760 --> 00:39:20,239
he must have loved her so much.

679
00:39:31,840 --> 00:39:33,000
From what I gather,

680
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:34,599
the designer of this beer label

681
00:39:35,079 --> 00:39:37,079
submitted it anonymously from Qingzhou.

682
00:39:39,039 --> 00:39:41,119
At first, I assumed they were from Qingzhou.

683
00:39:41,920 --> 00:39:43,960
But these past couple of days, it hit me.

684
00:39:44,519 --> 00:39:45,880
Submitting from Qingzhou

685
00:39:46,280 --> 00:39:47,920
doesn't mean they had to be a local.

686
00:39:48,840 --> 00:39:50,719
They could just be working in Qingzhou.

687
00:39:52,639 --> 00:39:53,320
Chen Yuan.

688
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:56,039
Back then,

689
00:39:57,079 --> 00:39:59,360
you worked at Qingzhou Normal University?

690
00:40:02,239 --> 00:40:04,280
Liu Xuemei was always running off to Qingzhou.

691
00:40:05,119 --> 00:40:06,679
She was going there to see you, wasn't she?

692
00:40:07,360 --> 00:40:08,039
Drop it.

693
00:40:08,880 --> 00:40:10,519
Going to Qingzhou to pay the deposit,

694
00:40:11,239 --> 00:40:12,360
she visited you then too, didn't she?

695
00:40:12,679 --> 00:40:13,679
Just stop asking!

696
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:17,079
You...

697
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:19,519
you're that lover of hers.

698
00:40:27,199 --> 00:40:27,920
Yes.

699
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:31,039
I'm the one who took the tapes from your place.

700
00:40:32,519 --> 00:40:34,000
All I wanted was to know

701
00:40:34,199 --> 00:40:35,920
how Xuemei really died.

702
00:40:36,199 --> 00:40:38,320
I've bottled this up for over a decade.

703
00:40:41,519 --> 00:40:42,880
Everyone dragged her name through the mud,

704
00:40:43,239 --> 00:40:44,360
but I never believed any of it.

705
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:47,679
Yet how did Xuemei actually die?

706
00:40:48,599 --> 00:40:49,800
She never touched alcohol.

707
00:40:50,079 --> 00:40:51,760
Why was she drunk that day?

708
00:40:52,880 --> 00:40:54,400
I desperately wanted to know,

709
00:40:57,239 --> 00:40:58,719
but had no way of finding out.

710
00:41:02,639 --> 00:41:03,840
Until by chance,

711
00:41:05,159 --> 00:41:06,519
I heard Xiaoqin mention

712
00:41:07,719 --> 00:41:09,639
that you had a lot of discarded footage.

713
00:41:11,360 --> 00:41:13,239
I figured Xuemei had to be in there.

714
00:41:15,519 --> 00:41:16,719
After all these years,

715
00:41:17,400 --> 00:41:19,000
I just wanted to see her.

716
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:24,440
That was my only pathetic thought.

717
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:32,159
In fact, I went looking for you before.

718
00:41:34,079 --> 00:41:35,280
I left you a note,

719
00:41:36,199 --> 00:41:37,159
asking to meet up.

720
00:41:39,119 --> 00:41:40,719
But when I showed up the next day,

721
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:43,079
I saw someone else was there.

722
00:41:44,079 --> 00:41:44,639
Stand right there!

723
00:41:45,679 --> 00:41:46,400
So later,

724
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:46,960
Don't move!

725
00:41:48,559 --> 00:41:50,239
I could only wait until you visited me

726
00:41:52,199 --> 00:41:53,320
to take the tapes.

727
00:42:27,599 --> 00:42:28,719
Do you know why

728
00:42:28,719 --> 00:42:30,400
beer bottles are always green?

729
00:42:32,239 --> 00:42:33,079
Why?

730
00:42:34,079 --> 00:42:35,320
In the late 19th century,

731
00:42:36,079 --> 00:42:38,280
brewers first started using glass bottles.

732
00:42:39,280 --> 00:42:41,920
Glassmaking wasn't very advanced back then.

733
00:42:43,199 --> 00:42:44,599
Too many ferrous ions

734
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:45,960
made the glass turn green.

735
00:42:46,559 --> 00:42:48,559
Later, when the technology improved,

736
00:42:49,639 --> 00:42:51,519
the quality of beer in clear bottles

737
00:42:51,599 --> 00:42:52,599
actually went downhill.

738
00:42:54,519 --> 00:42:56,159
Green glass blocked out the light,

739
00:42:56,599 --> 00:42:57,559
and it was cheaper,

740
00:42:58,440 --> 00:42:59,880
so they just rolled with the mistake.

741
00:43:01,440 --> 00:43:02,440
You know everything, don't you?

742
00:43:03,199 --> 00:43:04,039
You bet.

743
00:43:04,239 --> 00:43:05,400
I grew up around the smell of beer.

744
00:43:18,119 --> 00:43:18,760
All done.

745
00:43:19,079 --> 00:43:19,840
You can move now.

746
00:43:20,199 --> 00:43:21,079
You can move now.

747
00:43:27,639 --> 00:43:28,760
It's drawn really well.

748
00:43:40,519 --> 00:43:41,559
Then can you tell us

749
00:43:41,639 --> 00:43:43,840
why you erased what was on the tape?

750
00:43:44,960 --> 00:43:46,800
It really was an accident.

751
00:43:46,800 --> 00:43:48,760
Why would Chen Yuan erase this part?

752
00:43:49,119 --> 00:43:50,800
Is that Chen Qingchun in the distance?

753
00:43:51,199 --> 00:43:52,519
What's he holding in his hand?

754
00:43:52,840 --> 00:43:54,519
No one will ever know now.

755
00:43:56,280 --> 00:43:57,719
You can put your mind at ease.

756
00:43:58,239 --> 00:43:59,199
Feel free to check.

757
00:43:59,800 --> 00:44:00,920
Where were you the day Cao Jun died?

758
00:44:01,239 --> 00:44:01,880
Cao Jun?
